<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan yarn rates ease on low demand.</title>
<headline>Pakistan yarn rates ease on low demand.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton yarn rates eased on Wednesday on low demand, dealers said. Rates were likely to fall in the next few days, they added.</p>
<p>Following are the rates in rupees supplied by the Pakistan Yarn Merchants Association for 10-lb (4.54 kg) cone of 21 counts:			    Wednesday   Feb 16</p>
<p>    Suraiya Textile	    475	   485</p>
<p>    Taj Textile		  490	   500</p>
<p>    Globe			  490	   500</p>
<p>    Din Textile		  490	   495</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees) -- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
